&lt;h1 id=&#34;about&#34;&gt;About
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quarkdown is a modern Markdown-based typesetting system, designed around the key concept of &lt;strong&gt;versatility&lt;/strong&gt;, by seamlessly compiling a project
into a print-ready book or an interactive presentation.
All through an incredibly powerful Turing-complete extension of Markdown, ensuring your ideas flow automatically into paper.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://raw.githubusercontent.com/iamgio/quarkdown/project-files/images/paged-demo.png&#34; alt=&#34;Paper demo&#34;&gt;
  &lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Original credits: &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762v7&#34;&gt;Attention Is All You Need&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Born as an extension of CommonMark and GFM, the Quarkdown Flavor brings &lt;strong&gt;functions&lt;/strong&gt; to Markdown, along with many other syntax extensions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a function call:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;.somefunction {arg1} {arg2}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    Body argument
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Possibilities are unlimited&lt;/strong&gt; thanks to an ever-expanding &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;quarkdown-stdlib/src/main/kotlin/com/quarkdown/stdlib&#34; &gt;standard library&lt;/a&gt;,
which offers layout builders, I/O, math, conditional statements and loops.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not enough?&lt;/strong&gt; You can still define your own functions and variables — all within Markdown.
You can even create awesome libraries for everyone to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;.function {greet}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    to from:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    **Hello, .to** from .from!
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;.greet {world} from:{iamgio}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Result: &lt;strong&gt;Hello, world&lt;/strong&gt; from iamgio!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This out-of-the-box scripting support opens doors to complex and dynamic content that would be otherwise impossible
to achieve with vanilla Markdown.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Combined with live preview and :zap: fast compilation speed, Quarkdown simply gets the work done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
